// KNOWN LIMITATION — should verify, currently rejected.
//
// The range of an undecided `ite` is the hull of its arms' ranges, each arm
// taken whole. Here an arm is only reached where the condition holds — `level`
// in the inner else-arm is `>= 0`, and below `11` under the outer one — but the
// analysis does not narrow an arm by its condition: that would read the
// condition's operands, which are not the `ite`'s children, so the range would
// not be re-derived when they change (order-dependent). Narrowing each arm under
// its own path condition is the job of a join that evaluates arms in their
// context. Silicon verifies this (miniz `create_comp_flags_from_zip_params`).
// Unsound twins: `tests/cases/failing/intervals/clamp_upper.vpr`,
// `wrong_arm.vpr`.

method clamp(level: Int)
{
  var r: Int := level > 10 ? 10 : (level >= 0 ? level : 6)
  assert 0 <= r && r < 11
}
